A||||7||sqoach||What kind of tranny fluid for 4spd V6?||||5||
Z||000000||sqoach||09-04-2001||12:56 AM||||Topic says it all. Just wondering what everyone recommends.<P>------------------<BR>-Adam<BR><FONT COLOR="BLUE">sqoach@yahoo.com</FONT><BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sqoach.gif">        <BR>^^^^^^<B>new project</B>^^^^^^<BR><LI><FONT SIZE="1">84 SE (FOR SALE)*sale pending*<BR><LI>85 Coupe (parts car)($50)*sale pending*<BR><LI>86 SC (FOR SALE)</FONT>||||reg||5
Z||000001||Carrolles||09-04-2001||07:37 AM||||I use what the factory recommends.<P>5W30 motor oil.  I use Havoline.||||reg||1
Z||000002||rogergarrison||09-04-2001||07:54 AM||||yep, but i use Castrol||||reg||1
Z||000003||StuGood||09-04-2001||01:19 PM||||In case you need another vote, I've used the factory-recommended 5W-30 motor oil in my 1986 V6 SE 4-speed transaxle since I bought the car new.  Trans. has given no problems.   <BR> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||sqoach||09-04-2001||01:22 PM||||Oh, so you use motor oil for the engine and the tranny? My dad was telling me the tranny fluid is much thicker.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/confused.gif"><P>Oh yeah, do I always use the same kind, even when the miles get "up there"?? Right now it's at 82K.||||reg||1
Z||000005||artherd||09-04-2001||03:53 PM||||I have a Getrag 5-speed, but I use Redline MTL.  *Great* stuff. <P>  Motor oil, especially newer synthetics, is generally too slipry for proper syncro engagement.<P>The Redline product has special gunk added to make the syncros work, yet retain the excellent lube properties of a synthetic gear oil.<P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/88ttop.jpg">  <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top Metalic Red<BR>88 Formula, Silver<BR>87 Coupe, Metalic Red<BR>"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>                -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000006||Carrolles||09-04-2001||10:14 PM||||Don't use regular gear lube (hypoid oil) that your dad probably remembers from his hotrod days. It's way too thick.  Our transmissions need motor oil (at least that's what Pontiac calls for in my 85SE v-6 4spd).||||reg||1
Z||000007||gt boy||09-04-2001||10:19 PM||||i just changed mine to mobil 1 synthetic last weekend..seems to work fine so far...i think it also shifts a little smoother too.||||reg||1
